WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.140
The king of Savatthi once put on

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.090
a rather strange exhibition.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.290
A Buddhist text, the Udana,

4
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.070
tells it.

5
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.070
The king had every person in the

6
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.610
city who was blind from birth

7
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.290
brought together, and an

8
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.780
elephant brought in.

9
00:00:15.284 --> 00:00:16.924
To some he showed the head.

10
00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:19.904
To others, an ear, a tusk, the

11
00:00:19.904 --> 00:00:22.294
trunk, the body, a foot.

12
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:24.093
Then the king asked:

13
00:00:24.093 --> 00:00:26.093
what is an elephant like?

14
00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:28.473
Those who felt the head said, a

15
00:00:28.473 --> 00:00:29.593
water jar.

16
00:00:29.593 --> 00:00:32.353
The ear, a winnowing basket.

17
00:00:32.353 --> 00:00:34.643
The tusk, a plowshare.

18
00:00:35.126 --> 00:00:36.886
The trunk was a plow pole.

19
00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:39.346
The body, a storeroom.

20
00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:41.446
The foot, a post.

21
00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:43.546
The tail, a pestle.

22
00:00:43.546 --> 00:00:45.706
And the tuft at its end, a

23
00:00:45.706 --> 00:00:46.506
broom.

24
00:00:47.057 --> 00:00:48.487
Each was certain.

25
00:00:48.487 --> 00:00:50.917
An elephant is like this, not

26
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.917
like that!

27
00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.477
They ended up fighting with

28
00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:55.157
their fists, and the king was

29
00:00:55.157 --> 00:00:57.517
delighted. Nobody thought to ask

30
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:58.527
the elephant.

31
00:00:59.087 --> 00:01:00.927
In the text, the Buddha tells

32
00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.187
this to monks, about wanderers

33
00:01:03.187 --> 00:01:05.527
of rival sects who quarrel, each

34
00:01:05.527 --> 00:01:07.127
holding one view as the whole

35
00:01:07.127 --> 00:01:07.927
truth.

36
00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.930
His verse says:

37
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.510
those who see only one side of

38
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.766
things end up quarrelling.

39
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:16.506
For GS4:

40
00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:18.046
a single viewpoint, however

41
00:01:18.046 --> 00:01:21.246
sincere, is only part of the

42
00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:24.126
truth. Humility, and openness to

43
00:01:24.126 --> 00:01:26.576
other perspectives, begin there.

44
00:01:27.464 --> 00:01:29.444
The elephant, meanwhile, stood

45
00:01:29.444 --> 00:01:31.044
perfectly still.

46
00:01:31.044 --> 00:01:33.134
Somebody had to be sensible.
